abstract: >-
  GeoSpectra Lab is a falsification-first validation harness for
  discretized spectral operators on finite-lattice compact product
  toy manifolds. The Gate 4B v0.1.24 corrected campaign (216 cases,
  S³×S¹) plus negative-controls campaign v0.1.22 (54 cases) plus
  wilson-scrambled extension (18 cases) plus spectral-circle extension
  (18 cases) — 306 cases total — produced the FINAL verdict
  DISCRETIZATION_SENSITIVE / GEOMETRY_AGNOSTIC: the harness
  distinguishes lattice product structure from random / scrambled /
  broken baselines (specificity to Level 3 — FFT vs lattice
  discretization), but does NOT distinguish Wilson-term internal
  details (Level 5). Aggregate true-IPR contrast (W=20 vs W=0)
  preserved at 7.07× after S³ Dirac operator correction (versus
  7.15× before correction, change less than 1.1%). This is a
  methodology paper, NOT a physical compactification proof. All
  validation on finite-lattice toy operators (N ≤ 896). Eight
  scientific non-claims explicitly stated: no continuum
  compactification, no S⁶ or S³×S⁶ validation, no Standard Model
  derivation, no physical chirality, no Witten/Lichnerowicz bypass,
  no physical extra dimensions, no hierarchy solution, no observable
  predictions.
keywords:
  - falsification-first validation
  - spectral operators
  - compact manifolds
  - Anderson localization
  - Dirac operators
  - finite-lattice diagnostics
  - methodology
  - toy model validation
  - product manifolds
  - lattice field theory
  - differential geometry
  - numerical analysis
  - negative controls
  - discretization sensitivity
